WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.800
-Our first guest is

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:02.802
a Golden Globe winner

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:03.970
for his work on the

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:06.472
very popular series
"Brooklyn Nine-Nine."

00:00:06.472 --> 00:00:08.274
The eighth, and final, season

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:11.477
airs Thursdays at 8:00 pm,
right here on NBC.

00:00:11.477 --> 00:00:14.413
Here is Andy Samberg!
Andy!

00:00:14.413 --> 00:00:15.614
[ Cheering and applause ]
[ "Brooklyn Nine-Nine" theme
sting plays ]

00:00:15.614 --> 00:00:17.717
Wow.
That's what I'm talking about.

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:19.218 line:85%
[ Whistling ]

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:19.218
[ Laughing, clapping ]

00:00:19.218 --> 00:00:21.020
Yeah.
Feels like a long time,

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:23.423
but you were just here
before the commercial break.

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:25.024
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.024 --> 00:00:27.126
You look good, bud.
-Fond memories, for sure, yeah.

00:00:27.126 --> 00:00:28.795
How are ya?
-We had some great memories.

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:30.897
"Purple Rain," we should've got.

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:33.733
Hey, happy belated birthday.

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:35.068
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:37.437
Appreciate that.

00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:41.507
Did you do anything to celebrate
or anything special?

00:00:41.507 --> 00:00:43.208
-Well, I'm doing
a little bit of work,

00:00:43.208 --> 00:00:44.577
but I had a fun time.

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:47.079
I celebrated on the weekend
with my family.

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:49.115
-Aw.

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:51.183
I saw you have a little girl.

00:00:51.183 --> 00:00:53.486
-Yeah, my daughter's four
-Wow.

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:55.854 line:78%
[ Awwing ]

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:55.854
and she was really excited
for my birthday.

00:00:55.854 --> 00:01:00.860
She told me, first thing
on my birthday, you know, like,

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:03.963
"Do you think you would want
donuts for your birthday?"

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:05.765
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:08.868
And I was like,
"Do you want donuts

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:10.169
[ Laughter ]
for my birthday?"

00:01:10.169 --> 00:01:11.904
-That's where we're going.
-She was like, "I mean,

00:01:11.904 --> 00:01:16.042
if you got donuts
and there was a unicorn donut,

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:17.343
would you want that?

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:19.178
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.178 --> 00:01:20.679
-Of course I want that.
-So, yeah.

00:01:20.679 --> 00:01:22.548
I got her a unicorn donut
for my birthday.

00:01:22.548 --> 00:01:24.884
[ Laughter ]
-Four years old.

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:27.153
What do you play for music
around the house

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:29.188
for a four-year-old?

00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:31.458
-Mostly just like
Too Short, N.W.A.

00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:34.127
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, kids love, yeah.

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:35.161
New stuff, yeah.

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:36.796
Throw in some
Megan Thee Stallion.

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:38.431
[ Laughter ]
Like, you know, kid stuff.

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:41.501
Yeah, kid stuff. Cardi B.
Yeah, of course, kid stuff.

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:43.536
-Lot of that.
Lot of Korn.

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:46.739
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:49.943
Do you think about that
when you're playing songs, now,

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:51.711
for your daughter
and you're like,

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:54.814
"That's not the best song
for you to be liking"?

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:57.216
-I mean, it's either that
or KIDZ BOP, right?

00:01:57.216 --> 00:02:00.053
[ Laughter ]
-That's true.
I don't mind a good KIDZ BOP.

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:02.322
-I want to get just
instrumentals of everything

00:02:02.322 --> 00:02:04.791
and then like see
what she freestyles over.

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:07.827
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:09.862
-Start 'em young.

00:02:09.862 --> 00:02:11.297
-I grew up --
I have older sisters

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:13.232
and I would listen
to all their music.

00:02:13.232 --> 00:02:15.535
I feel like I was like seven
or eight when I was like

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:17.470
listening
to Eazy E's first album.

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.372
[ Laughter ]
And I think about that now

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:21.908
and I'm like, "Goddamn!"
-Yeah.

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:23.109
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:24.210
"I probably shouldn't
have heard that!"

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.279
But, you know,
it worked out fine.

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:27.746
And they're good beats.

00:02:27.746 --> 00:02:30.883
-I remember having that cassette
and like hiding it

00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:32.651
like under my bed or something.

00:02:32.651 --> 00:02:34.119
I didn't want like --
I was like,

00:02:34.119 --> 00:02:36.555
"Oh, this is the filthiest thing
I've ever heard in my life."

00:02:36.555 --> 00:02:38.258
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, my parents,

00:02:38.258 --> 00:02:40.459
we would play it in the car
and my parents would be like,

00:02:40.459 --> 00:02:42.428
"I don't know,"
but they didn't make us stop.

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:44.230
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.532
-That's not true at all.

00:02:46.532 --> 00:02:48.034
-Well, my dad
didn't make us stop.

00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:50.069
My mom would not have
let it happen.

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:51.704
-Yeah.

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:52.972
You got a bunch
of things going on,

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:55.107
but I want to talk to you
about you and John Mulaney

00:02:55.107 --> 00:02:58.477
are going to be the new voices
of Chip 'n Dale

00:02:58.477 --> 00:02:59.979
[ Cheering and applause ]
in the new "Chip 'n Dale" movie.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:01.781
-Yeah.

00:03:01.781 --> 00:03:03.182
-We love Mulaney.

00:03:03.182 --> 00:03:04.317
How cool is that?

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:08.221
Now, voicing Dale,
pressure's on.

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:09.923
Do want to give us a taste,
maybe a debut,

00:03:09.923 --> 00:03:12.592
of what the Dale voice
will be like?

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:14.560
-Yeah, well, it's a long
legacy, obviously,

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:16.596
with the "Rescue Rangers"

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:18.230
and my buddy Akiva
was directing,

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:19.899
that's how it all sort of
got started.

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:21.267
-Okay.
-I feel like

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.802
I was a little let down because,
when he asked me to do it,

00:03:23.802 --> 00:03:25.305
I was like,
"Oh, I'm going to like work

00:03:25.305 --> 00:03:27.473
on my chipmunk voice," you know?

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:28.607
So I was like at home like --

00:03:28.607 --> 00:03:30.143
[ Squeakily ]
Blah blah blah blah.

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:32.111
[ Laughter ]
-[ Clapping ]

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:33.980
Yeah! That's fantastic!

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:36.648
[ Applause ]
That is great!

00:03:36.648 --> 00:03:39.985
-But, then I started doing that
and he's like, "No!

00:03:39.985 --> 00:03:42.155
Just do your voice.
What are you doing?"

00:03:42.155 --> 00:03:43.756
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:46.158
-So you're just doing you?

00:03:46.158 --> 00:03:49.195
-Yeah, it's an interesting take.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:50.996
It's almost like
a Roger Rabbit sitch,

00:03:50.996 --> 00:03:51.997
the new "Rescue Rangers."

00:03:51.997 --> 00:03:53.199
-Oh!
-It's like two live

00:03:53.199 --> 00:03:55.234
in the real world with people.

00:03:55.234 --> 00:04:00.873
And so we're we're Chip 'n Dale
like the cartoon actors.

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:02.808
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah. Dude, that's fantastic!

00:04:02.808 --> 00:04:03.810
-It's going to be really fun.

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:04.977
Yeah.
-That's legendary, dude.

00:04:04.977 --> 00:04:06.379
Congrats on that.
That's super fun.

00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:07.680
-Thank you.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:10.116
-I want to talk to you
about "Brooklyn Nine-Nine."

00:04:10.116 --> 00:04:11.684
This is the eighth
and final season.

00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:13.953
Congrats on the long run,
by the way.

00:04:13.953 --> 00:04:14.954
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:17.523
-That's legit.
-Thanks.

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:21.093
It's legit. It's on Thursdays
at 8:00 here at NBC.

00:04:21.093 --> 00:04:25.565
Did it get emotional,
those last couple episodes?

00:04:25.565 --> 00:04:27.633
-Yeah, for sure.
I mean, you know,

00:04:27.633 --> 00:04:30.569
eight years
of doing the same job,

00:04:30.569 --> 00:04:32.438
you get really attached
to the people,

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:36.442
you feel like family and --

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:39.678
You know, it was basically
like a week-long

00:04:39.678 --> 00:04:41.547
mental and emotional breakdown,

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:43.616
the last week, I would say.
-Yeah.

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:45.418
-♪ Arrest,
arrest, arrest, arrest ♪

00:04:45.418 --> 00:04:46.852
♪ Arrest, arrest,
arrest, arrest ♪

00:04:46.852 --> 00:04:48.554
♪ Arrest,
arrest, arrest, arrest ♪

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:51.057
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.057 --> 00:04:53.459
-Did you --

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:56.295
♪♪
Did you hear that as well?

00:04:56.295 --> 00:04:59.331
[ Laughter ]

00:04:59.331 --> 00:05:02.134
-Uh, are we in the Matrix?

00:05:02.134 --> 00:05:03.602
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:03.602 --> 00:05:07.006
-Hey, would you know
if I'm having a heart attack?

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:09.642
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:11.077
-That was a digital
heart attack.

00:05:11.077 --> 00:05:13.178
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.178 --> 00:05:15.848
-One of us is a robot.

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:18.117
♪ Arrest, arrest,
arrest, arrest ♪

00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:19.185
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.185 --> 00:05:20.419
Like Max Headroom.

00:05:20.419 --> 00:05:22.254
-♪ Cardiac arrest,
arrest, arrest, arrest ♪

00:05:22.254 --> 00:05:24.022
[ Laughter ]
♪ Cardiac arrest, arrest ♪

00:05:24.022 --> 00:05:26.258
Alright. Wow, wow, wow.
-P-P-P-P-Pepsi.

00:05:26.258 --> 00:05:27.660
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.962
-Dude, classic
"Max Headroom" ref.

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:31.530
-Classic Headroom!

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:34.233
-That's so classic Headroom,
dude. I got it.

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:36.869
-Ironically, didn't have
a lot of headroom in his shot.

00:05:36.869 --> 00:05:38.071
[ Laughter ]
It was a pretty tight frame.

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:39.772
-Yeah, it wasn't the maximum,
at least.

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:41.607
It was probably the minimum.

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:44.911
[ Laughter ]
It's like Min Headroom.

00:05:44.911 --> 00:05:46.912
-Min Headroom!
That was the prequel.

00:05:46.912 --> 00:05:49.348
[ Laughter ]
-That's correct.

00:05:49.348 --> 00:05:51.850
I want to tell everyone
to tune in

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:53.953
and watch "Brooklyn Nine-Nine"
for this last season.

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:56.055
And I want
to congratulate you again.

00:05:56.055 --> 00:05:58.491
Not only is it super funny,
but I also thought it was

00:05:58.491 --> 00:06:00.526
such a positive show as well.

00:06:00.526 --> 00:06:01.927
-Thanks.
-It always put me
in a great mood.

00:06:01.927 --> 00:06:04.463
The whole cast, top to bottom,
everyone was great.

00:06:04.463 --> 00:06:06.565
So congrats on that, buddy.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:06.565 --> 00:06:09.001
Here's Andy Samberg
in "Brooklyn Nine-Nine."

00:06:09.001 --> 00:06:10.069
Take a look.

00:06:10.069 --> 00:06:11.837
-I'm initiating
Operation Trident.

00:06:11.837 --> 00:06:13.773
-Cool, just like
the sugarless gum,

00:06:13.773 --> 00:06:15.307
because we're going
to chew them up.

00:06:15.307 --> 00:06:18.043
-No, like the famed weapon
of the sea,

00:06:18.043 --> 00:06:20.779
forged by the Cyclops
for Poseidon himself.

00:06:20.779 --> 00:06:23.983
The trident has three prongs,
like my approach.

00:06:23.983 --> 00:06:26.652
-Not to interrupt, but Aquaman's
trident has five prongs.

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:28.053
-That's absurd.

00:06:28.053 --> 00:06:30.155
The prefix tri- means "three."

00:06:30.155 --> 00:06:32.858
What this Aquatic Man carries
is better termed a pentadactyl.

00:06:32.858 --> 00:06:34.593
-No, it's a trident.
They call it that

00:06:34.593 --> 00:06:36.928
in the original theatrical
release and the Snyder cut,

00:06:36.928 --> 00:06:39.232
so you're 100% wrong
and everyone's laughing at you.

00:06:39.232 --> 00:06:41.601
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:06:41.601 --> 00:06:43.168
Everyone's laughing at you.

00:06:43.168 --> 00:06:44.970
I don't know. Yeah.

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:47.707
-Snyder cut.
-Congrats on the success
of that.

00:06:47.707 --> 00:06:49.509
Also, this is exciting --
I heard that you're

00:06:49.509 --> 00:06:51.543
already working
on a brand-new show.

00:06:51.543 --> 00:06:55.014
You're actually
on one of the sets now.

00:06:55.014 --> 00:06:57.416
Can you tell us
about the new show?

00:06:57.416 --> 00:06:59.184
-I can, yes.

00:06:59.184 --> 00:07:02.654
It's a cooking competition show
called "Baking It,"

00:07:02.654 --> 00:07:04.323
produced by our friend
Amy Poehler,

00:07:04.323 --> 00:07:06.324
and I'm cohosting
with Maya Rudolph.

00:07:06.324 --> 00:07:08.794
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Are you kidding me?! Come on!

00:07:08.794 --> 00:07:10.596
♪♪
Oh, my gosh!

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:11.864
I love you guys!

00:07:11.864 --> 00:07:14.099
Holy moly!

00:07:14.099 --> 00:07:15.500
Stay safe, you guys.

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:17.102
I love it.
Andy Samberg,

00:07:17.102 --> 00:07:18.805
Amy Poehler, Maya Rudolph.

00:07:18.805 --> 00:07:19.939
[ Cheering and applause ]
-[ Laughing ]

00:07:19.939 --> 00:07:21.773
-Catch back-to-back episodes

00:07:21.773 --> 00:07:24.877
of "Brooklyn Nine-Nine"
Thursdays at 8:00 pm on NBC.

